    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0258" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1347.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-24T22:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1912—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bankers to-day submitted plan sent from London for supervision and control of
                    loan expenditures, including foreign administration of salt gabelle, to the
                    Minister of Finance. The plan was emphatically rejected. It is not anticipated
                    that any adequate control can be secured. Apparently groups will have to break
                    off negotiations for a while at least.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
